  "origin": "BLOOM is a 176-billion-parameter decoder-only Transformer language model trained on ROOTS (1.6TB, 59 languages, 498 datasets). The model is released under the BigScience RAIL (Responsible AI License) v1.0 — a license that is open and permissive in copyright/patent grants but carries use-based restrictions (Attachment A of the license) prohibiting specific harmful uses (e.g. exploiting minors, generating verifiably false information to harm others, fully automated decision-making adversely impacting legal rights, discrimination against protected groups, providing medical advice, use in law-enforcement/immigration/asylum processes). The license field points at the RAIL License v1.0 text directly. This is a distinct licensing model from pure open-source (Apache 2.0) or pure data licenses (CC0/CC-BY): a model license with use-restriction clauses. The 0.0.1 schema's single `license` IRI points at the license text but cannot express that the license has use-based restrictions layered on top of copyright/patent grants — an auditor following the IRI finds the full license text, so the claim is checkable, but the license is not classifiable into a standard category (open-source / open-data / restricted) from the IRI alone. See notes/stress-test-bloom-roots.md (Gap G discussion). The training data (ROOTS) is not licensed under the RAIL License; it is a separate corpus with its own (heterogeneous, agreement-supplied) licensing documented in the ROOTS records. BLOOM was released with open-access weights under the RAIL License, not as a fully open model in the OSI sense.",
